sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Runbook reuse and exploratory resolution
  accDescr: In runbook-aware mode, an eligible known-good runbook can bypass LLM reasoning. Otherwise the workflow retrieves context and asks the LLM for a proposal. Both paths use local simulated actions and persist the relevant memory updates.
  autonumber
  participant User
  participant Flow as Workflow
  participant Memory as Local stores
  participant LLM
  participant Actions as Simulated actions

  User->>Flow: Submit support query
  Flow->>Memory: Find matching runbook
  Memory-->>Flow: Candidate, similarity, and history
  Flow->>Flow: Check status and reuse policy
  alt Known-good match and policy approved
    Note over Flow,LLM: Fast path skips the LLM
    Flow->>Actions: Execute saved steps
    Actions-->>Flow: Structured simulated result
    Flow->>Memory: Record runbook usage and status
  else No eligible match or reuse policy rejected
    Flow->>Memory: Retrieve documents and past cases
    Memory-->>Flow: Context and case history
    Flow->>LLM: Propose action with context
    LLM-->>Flow: Action, confidence, and risk
    Flow->>Flow: Resolve, partially automate, or escalate
    Flow->>Actions: Execute selected action or escalation
    Actions-->>Flow: Structured simulated result
    Flow->>Memory: Save case and eligible runbook candidate
  end
  Flow-->>User: Outcome, path, and execution metrics
